e:】  | 【26†plant metabolite】  Any eukaryotic metabolite produced during a metabolic reaction in plants, the kingdom that include flowering plants, conifers and other gymnosperms.\nL57: 【27†Application s:】  | 【28†antineoplastic agent】  A substance that inhibits or prevents the proliferation of neoplasms.【29†refrigerant】  A substance used in a thermodynamic heat pump cycle or refrigeration cycle that undergoes a phase change from a gas to a liquid and back.\nL58: Refrigerants are used in air-conditioning systems and freezers or refrigerators and are assigned a \"R\" number (by ASHRAE - formerly the American Society of Heating, Refrigerating and Air Conditioning Engineers), which is determined systematically according to their molecular structure.\nL59: ChEBI Ontology\nL60: ---\nL61: \nL62: Text\nL63: \nL64: Tree View\nL65: \nL66: Graph View\nL67: Outgoing Relation(s)\nL68: ethane (【30†CHEBI:42266】) has role antineoplastic agent (【28†CHEBI:35610】)\nL69: ethane (【30†CHEBI:42266】) has role plant metabolite (【26†CHEBI:76924】)\nL70: ethane (【30†CHEBI:42266】) has role refrigerant (【29†CHEBI:78433】)\nL71: ethane (【30†CHEBI:42266】) is a alkane (【31†CHEBI:18310】)\nL72: ethane (【30†CHEBI:42266】) is a gas molecular entity (【32†CHEBI:138675】)\nL73: Incoming Relation(s)\nL74: chloroethanes (【33†CHEBI:36016】) has parent hydride ethane (【30†CHEBI:42266】)\nL75: ethyl (【34†CHEBI:62801】) has parent hydride ethane (【30†CHEBI:42266】)\nL76: ethylenediamine (【35†CHEBI:30347】) has parent hydride ethane (【30†CHEBI:42266】)\nL77: iodoethane (【36†CHEBI:42487】) has parent hydride ethane (【30†CHEBI:42266】)\nL78: ethyl group (【37†CHEBI:37807】) is substituent group from ethane (【30†CHEBI:42266】)\nL79: ethylene group (【38†CHEBI:29362】) is substituent group from ethane (【30†CHEBI:42266】)\nL80: ethylidene group (【39†CHEBI:29853】) is substituent group from ethane (【30†CHEBI:42266】)\nL81: IUPAC Name\nL82: ---\nL83: ethane\nL84: \nL85: Synonym s   | Source\nL86: --- | ---\nL87: Äthan  | ChEBI\nL88: bimet