ied  | 20 November 2019\nL27: Downloads  | 【14†Molfile】\nL28: \nL29: On this page\nL30:   * 【15†Intro】\nL31:   * 【16†Roles Classification】\nL32:   * 【17†Ontology】\nL33:   * 【18†Names】\nL34:   * 【19†Manual Xrefs】\nL35:   * 【20†Registry Numbers】\nL36:   * 【21†Citations】\nL37: \nL38: Formula  | CH4\nL39: Net Charge  | 0\nL40: Average Mass  | 16.043\nL41: Monoisotopic Mass  | 16.03130\nL42: SMILES  | [H]C([H])([H])[H]\nL43: InChI  | InChI=1S/CH4/h1H4\nL44: InChIKey  | VNWKTOKETHGBQD-UHFFFAOYSA-N\nL45: \nL46: Wikipedia\nL47: ---\nL48: \nL49: Roles Classification\nL50: ---\nL51: 【22†Chemical Role:】  | 【23†greenhouse gas】  A gas in an atmosphere that absorbs and emits radiation within the thermal infrared range, so contributing to the 'greenhouse effect'.\nL52: 【24†Biological Role:】  | 【25†bacterial metabolite】  Any prokaryotic metabolite produced during a metabolic reaction in bacteria.\nL53: 【26†Application:】  | 【27†fossil fuel】  A fuel such as coal, oil and natural gas which has formed over many years through the decomposition of deposited vegetation which was under extreme pressure of an overburden of earth.\nL54: ChEBI Ontology\nL55: ---\nL56: \nL57: Text\nL58: \nL59: Tree View\nL60: \nL61: Graph View\nL62: Outgoing Relation(s)\nL63: methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】) has role bacterial metabolite (【25†CHEBI:76969】)\nL64: methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】) has role fossil fuel (【27†CHEBI:35230】)\nL65: methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】) has role greenhouse gas (【23†CHEBI:76413】)\nL66: methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】) is a alkane (【29†CHEBI:18310】)\nL67: methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】) is a gas molecular entity (【30†CHEBI:138675】)\nL68: methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】) is a mononuclear parent hydride (【31†CHEBI:37176】)\nL69: methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】) is a one-carbon compound (【32†CHEBI:64708】)\nL70: methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】) is conjugate acid of methanide (【33†CHEBI:29438】)\nL71: Incoming Relation(s)\nL72: halomethane (【34†CHEBI:39279】) has parent hydride methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】)\nL73: hydridocarbon(•) (【35†CHEBI:29430】) has parent hydride methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】)\nL74: methanetriyl (【36†CHEBI:29431】) has parent hydride methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】)\nL75: methanimine (【37†CHEBI:38220】) has parent hydride methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】)\nL76: methyl (【38†CHEBI:29309】) has parent hydride methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】)\nL77: methane clathrate (【39†CHEBI:132140】) has part methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】)\nL78: methanide (【33†CHEBI:29438】) is conjugate base of methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】)\nL79: methanediylidene group (【40†CHEBI:30040】) is substituent group from methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】)\nL80: methanetetrayl group (【41†CHEBI:30039】) is substituent group from methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】)\nL81: methanetriyl group (【42†CHEBI:29433】) is substituent group from methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】)\nL82: methanylylidene group (【43†CHEBI:29432】) is substituent group from methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】)\nL83: methyl group (【44†CHEBI:32875】) is substituent group from methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】)\nL84: methylene group (【45†CHEBI:50728】) is substituent group from methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】)\nL85: methylidene group (【46†CHEBI:29358】) is substituent group from methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】)\nL86: methylidyne group (【47†CHEBI:29429】) is substituent group from methane (【28†CHEBI:16183】)\nL87: IUPAC Name s\nL88: ---\nL89: methane\nL90: tetrahydridocarbon\nL91: \nL92: Synonym s   | Source\nL93: --- | ---\nL94: CH_{4}  | IUPAC\nL95: marsh gas  | NIST Chemistry WebBook\nL96: metano  | ChEBI\nL97: Methan  | ChEBI\nL98: Methane  | KEGG COMPOUND\nL99: méthane  | ChEBI\nL100: \nL101: [Button: Show All]\nL102: \nL103: UniProt Name   | Source\nL104: --- | ---\nL105: methane  | UniProt\nL106: Manual Xrefs  | Databases\nL107: --- | ---\nL108: 【48†c0095†bioregistry.io】  | UM-BBD\nL109: 【49†C01438†bioregistry.io】  | KEGG COMPOUND\nL110: 【50†CH4†bioregistry.io】  | MetaCyc\nL111: 【51†FR994032†worldwide.espacenet.com】  | Patent\nL112: 【52†HMDB0002714†bioregistry.io】  | HMDB\nL113: 【53†Methane†bioregistry.io】  | Wikipedia\nL114: 【54†US2583090†wor