NJV-UHFFFAOYSA-N\nL45: \nL46: Roles Classification\nL47: ---\nL48: 【22†Chemical Role:】  | 【23†Bronsted acid】  A molecular entity capable of donating a hydron to an acceptor (Brønsted base).\nL49: 【24†Biological Role s:】  | 【25†plant metabolite】  Any eukaryotic metabolite produced during a metabolic reaction in plants, the kingdom that include flowering plants, conifers and other gymnosperms.【26†mammalian metabolite】  Any animal metabolite produced during a metabolic reaction in mammals.\nL50: \nL51: ChEBI Ontology\nL52: ---\nL53: \nL54: Text\nL55: \nL56: Tree View\nL57: \nL58: Graph View\nL59: Outgoing Relation(s)\nL60: isovaleric acid (【27†CHEBI:28484】) has role mammalian metabolite (【26†CHEBI:75768】)\nL61: isovaleric acid (【27†CHEBI:28484】) has role plant metabolite (【25†CHEBI:76924】)\nL62: isovaleric acid (【27†CHEBI:28484】) is a branched-chain saturated fatty acid (【28†CHEBI:39417】)\nL63: isovaleric acid (【27†CHEBI:28484】) is a methylbutyric acid (【29†CHEBI:38653】)\nL64: isovaleric acid (【27†CHEBI:28484】) is a short-chain fatty acid (【30†CHEBI:26666】)\nL65: isovaleric acid (【27†CHEBI:28484】) is conjugate acid of isovalerate (【31†CHEBI:48942】)\nL66: Incoming Relation(s)\nL67: (E)-2-(methoxyimino)-3-methylbutanoic acid (【32†CHEBI:131390】) has functional parent isovaleric acid (【27†CHEBI:28484】)\nL68: N-isovaleryl-L-alanine (【33†CHEBI:136818】) has functional parent isovaleric acid (【27†CHEBI:28484】)\nL69: O-isovalerylcarnitine (【34†CHEBI:73025】) has functional parent isovaleric acid (【27†CHEBI:28484】)\nL70: 2-(4-chlorophenyl)-3-methylbutyric acid (【35†CHEBI:39345】) has functional parent isovaleric acid (【27†CHEBI:28484】)\nL71: 2-(4-hydroxyphenyl)-3-methylbutyric acid (【36†CHEBI:39359】) has functional parent isovaleric acid (【27†CHEBI:28484】)\nL72: 2-hexenyl isovalerate (【37†CHEBI:176332】) has functional parent isovaleric acid (【27†CHEBI:28484】)\nL73: 2-hydroxy-3-methylbutyric acid (【38†CHEBI:60645】) has functional parent isovaleric acid (【27†CHEBI:28484】)\nL74: 2,2-